cff-version: 1.2.0
title: KiriChess
message: If you cite this variant or use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gekiere
    given-names: Michiel
# repository-code: set to the public snapshot URL once AD.13 ships; the working tree stays private.
url: https://kirichess.com
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
date-released: "2026-07-21"
abstract: >
  An original chess variant where the clock is a resource: captures, moves,
  and checks add or remove time. Invented by Michiel Gekiere in February 2026.
  First commit 2026-07-21 under the working title Clockstarved; later renamed
  KiriChess. Licensing is split: the software is Apache-2.0, and the rules
  manual (docs/RULES.md, config/kirichess.rules.json) is CC BY 4.0. See
  NOTICE in the repository for the full split, including the vendored
  GPL-3.0 engine and third-party assets.
